{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKP4m99j1LMVPkTHEtN4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BgP6sm7dV9sRVJBXD1wJVb","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core","path":"api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api","since":"2026-04-14","perPage":100},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308,"cache_read_input_tokens":13527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":308},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cbe038f-9f62-4368-916e-b7e56f4e6014","uuid":"3d480442-3d03-4d80-b53c-20c6cdf3fec7","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:09:57.601Z","request_id":"req_011CgKP4koZhBWc69jpgSyDi","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BgP6sm7dV9sRVJBXD1wJVb":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core","path":"api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api","since":"2026-04-14","perPage":100}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BgP6sm7dV9sRVJBXD1wJVb","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BgP6sm7dV9sRVJBXD1wJVb","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"5eb8cba2e30befeaec8ab7892dff14ac7dcc9d87\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:37:18+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException (#6674)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD, origin/master, origin/HEAD, master\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException\\n\\nSince TRUNK-6799, AuthorizationAdvice and core's explicit privilege\\nchecks denied with Spring Security's AccessDeniedException rather than\\nAPIAuthenticationException. Code catching the old type stopped\\nrecognizing denials; webservices.rest maps only that type, so REST\\nanswered 500 where it answered 401 or 403.\\n\\nAPIAuthenticationException now extends AuthorizationDeniedException.\\nCore throws it again wherever it did before 3.0.0, and wherever a\\n@PreAuthorize or @PostAuthorize check names the missing privilege, so a\\ncatch on either type recognizes the denial. It stays deprecated in\\nfavour of AccessDeniedException, which every denial is.\\n\\nIt is no longer an APIException, so a module compiled against an earlier\\ncore whose bytecode treats it as one fails verification until rebuilt.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6823: Deny a failed isAuthenticated() with APIAuthenticationException too\\n\\n@PreAuthorize(\\\"isAuthenticated()\\\"), the migration guide's translation of a\\nno-value @Authorized, denied a logged-out caller with a plain\\nAuthorizationDeniedException where @Authorized throws\\nAPIAuthenticationException, so converting such a method changed what its\\ncallers catch. It now records the denial for\\nPrivilegeNamingAuthorizationManager to report as AuthorizationAdvice does.\\n\\nTestInstallUtil throws APIAuthenticationException again, as before 3.0.0,\\nand the migration guide notes that the class is no longer an APIException.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0e0255b872f08dabafe9414d623820272cd475be\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:24:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6827: Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor (#6637)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor\\n\\nFixes #6636\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Keep the outbox from enqueueing events about its own rows\\n\\nNow that onPersist reaches EventInterceptor, saving an OutboxEvent row\\npublishes a SaveDbEvent about that row. With an @OutboxEventListener\\nthat accepts it, such as one taking SaveDbEvent<?> or EntityEvent<?>,\\nOutboxEventInterceptor saved another OutboxEvent for it, and so on,\\nuntil the JVM ran out of heap on the first create or update.\\nOutboxEventInterceptor now ignores entity events whose entity is an\\nOutboxEvent.\\n\\nThe new ChainingInterceptor overrides are @since 3.0.0, because 2.9.x\\nbuilds against Hibernate 5.6, whose Interceptor has no onPersist or\\nonRemove.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Stop auditing OutboxEvent with Envers\\n\\nWith hibernate.integration.envers.enabled=true, Envers writes the audit\\nrow of each new or changed OutboxEvent just before the transaction\\ncommits, with persist(entityName, Map). The SaveDbEvent for that row has\\na HashMap as its entity, so the OutboxEvent check in\\nOutboxEventInterceptor let it through to a listener such as one taking\\nSaveDbEvent<?>. That saved another OutboxEvent, whose audit row came\\nnext, and so on, with each payload nesting the previous one. On H2 the\\ncommit ended in OutOfMemoryError. On MySQL it ended in \\\"Data too long\\nfor column 'payload'\\\", so logins and the outbox poller failed.\\n\\nOutboxEvent is no longer @Audited, as on 2.9.x.\\nEnversAuditTableInitializerDatabaseIT expected an audit table for every\\nentity with an @Audited superclass, but Envers does not audit\\nOutboxEvent through BaseOpenmrsObject's annotation, so the test now\\nchecks the entity's own annotation.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"cb6cda4236b21a84cc4e1765a0dbaa58fdbe2565\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T15:17:25+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6802 Extend hasPermission to support custom rules provided from modules (#6668)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0340ada6bd4209e38630ebe7978041e0b514f85c\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T14:08:49+03:00\",\"message\":\"Initialize Context's user context holder before its logger (#6672)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes #6670\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"83411b2f8a52325e867fccc223a54d6a6f701400\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T22:20:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6819: Start the JobRunr job server only once OpenMRS has started (#6654)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The background job server was started while its application context was\\nstill being created, so jobs could run before the context was ready. On\\njetty:run this logged \\\"EntityManagerFactory is closed\\\" for a job that ran\\nduring the context refresh after modules start, against the closed session\\nfactory of the context being replaced, and \\\"Task class ... not found\\\" for a\\nmodule's job that ran after the first, core-only refresh, before modules\\nwere loaded.\\n\\nThe server is now started by a SmartLifecycle once its context has finished\\nrefreshing and stopped before the context closes. The webapp defers that\\nstart until SchedulerService.onStartup(), which runs once modules have\\nstarted; contexts refreshed after startup start their server right away.\\n\\nThe webapp never closes its application context, so Context.shutdown() now\\ncalls SchedulerService.onShutdown() first, as it did before the move to\\nJobRunr, and JobRunrSchedulerService stops the job server there, before the\\nmodules and the session factory are shut down.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NK4kFG8qyevx9Bk9jWoEgS\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PdDdZrB8Q5eMgej5FmRx4R\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZ92BDLHrn6xACczVMtSiR\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"41c5821a9b8b2d184207c8842e4c4331e02aaa7f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T21:27:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType (#6633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType\\n\\nFixes #6632\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Document that modules map their enums with StringEnumType\\n\\nThe class Javadoc said to delete StringEnumType once Obs, ConceptName\\nand OrderSet move to annotations. Modules now map their own enums with\\nit, so say that instead.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ja9UqKCQ2eMd7FaYQ2ewqz\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b64e0729cce60c40dffb75788c4b43937a6fc77e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T08:23:37-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6818: Context.closeSession() closes sessions it did not open (#6651)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2c9b2ee0dd005f64fa543ca8228c51f57cb319c7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T10:15:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6810: Extend cluster-safety to RolePrivilegeCache (#6627)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"07e8ea06f244de96907581535d4eff8dadbd0004\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:26:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6707: Implement full caching for Global Properties (#6598)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b147e0dcae701feb4670b53a454daf0cfb210ee9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T16:07:23+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6684: Location.childLocations gained unintended orphanRemoval=true in the JPA migration (#6444)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Wikum Weerakutti <wikum@linuxdeveloper.space>\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f10e3fb9a645378ab6682c21d6be478bfdab6199\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T16:28:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6721: Replace StackWalker with a thread-local guard in UserDAO (#6588)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"34bd26a8166d1277f83e4fdf1bda550ff8cc49a6\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T22:26:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6686: Restore relevance weighting in patient search lost in the Hibernate Search 6 migration (#6430)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3310bc1d9682151ac461faf0916ca3da7d5a88d0\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T14:06:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Follow-up: Re-add null privilege check and add guards\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1d0fb13892759020f6bc0824a097518d546024eb\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T13:45:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Reduce the overhead of the gzip filter (#6505)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6d787a1e60899e39377ce5011b298a188b3354c6\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T13:54:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6780: Add a MariaDB option to the test container harness (#6474)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit 5983a2b85e60caf1fdf7edaa8abc860d9f1dd17d)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6e77bfd03ab134fc7d66a0e3140d6e468f569ec5\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T11:39:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6697: HandlerUtil's cache should not be garbage collected (#6494)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ac1bd8778fc13247eb712a6cd7a949461cccdb6b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T07:58:28-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6662: Get unchanged password hashing working using Spring's interfaces (#6219)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit d58b63501b7fedd1e6b02981262d73122b967621)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d92b490aaa25fbd255be0d08a04da4772a03e3b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-22T01:13:29+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6756: Remove deprecated Daemon thread-execution overloads (#6483)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"tejas\",\"authorEmail\":\"tejaswaghmare.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d222c6085bbe13f62be68908ad9c3abbaa75db1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T12:44:57-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6729:  Let batch loading engage on the identifier and concept search paths (#6420)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Rohith Gurram\",\"authorEmail\":\"89861100+Rocker810@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2ce847744295132bbe5fb97f369fab714f09b309\",\"date\":\"2026-08-20T19:57:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6731: Add paging support to the obs retrieval API (#6410)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8bb5c2e9e36ab8fb09f0053786bc0f040775cc1e\",\"date\":\"2026-08-11T20:49:53+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6733: Use java-uuid-generator for entity UUIDs instead of UUID.randomUUID() (#6391)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Sathieskumar Sudeshkar\",\"authorEmail\":\"sudeshkar008sk@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1b5421a9a8d69030adb91124c3f9cb758dbc58a8\",\"date\":\"2026-07-24T11:14:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6712: Cache flattened role privileges for privilege and superuser checks (#6383)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"befcc055a108c28458fc21ff73f07dfe844f78a4\",\"date\":\"2026-07-24T10:16:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"Improve test suite run time (#6377)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1f6cc621cb7bf97dc4283b0c808f96373d90054f\",\"date\":\"2026-07-22T15:41:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6711: Batch-load search result pages (#6363)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9e011e2c09db99fd5cae20821e203fe9cc5f036b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T23:50:01+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6681: Improve LocationSearchCriteria query performance with pagination (#6359)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"omeri innocent\",\"authorEmail\":\"innocentomeri08@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"265582974b2589ffc8787b57c2e4ba0368cb6cba\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T12:44:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6713: Follow-up: Comment clean-up\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This was already included in the backports\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b68355b3dd934c7d5be3708d6637dfae8f845ee5\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T11:26:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6713: Switch to saner DaemonThread protection scheme (#6349)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"41ec2955656c6d7131c628d122d8c503b09c4cb1\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T10:37:09-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6694 & TRUNK-6695: Avoid synchronization in service fetching (#6348)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"50810cfb4d919602fa727eb78607675e2a5e3ec0\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T01:25:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"Require Get Patient Programs privilege for by-uuid program lookups (#6318)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Require Get Patient Programs privilege for by-uuid program lookups\\n\\nProgramWorkflowService.getPatientProgramByUuid and getPatientStateByUuid\\nhad no @Authorized annotation. Because AuthorizationAdvice only enforces\\nwhen a method declares a privilege, both fell through with no check at\\nall, letting any authenticated user read program-enrollment PHI by uuid.\\nEvery other read on the service, including getPatientProgram(Integer),\\nalready requires Get Patient Programs; annotate both by-uuid methods to\\nmatch.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Require Get Patient Programs privilege for patient program attribute lookup\\n\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName returns patient program\\nattribute values keyed by patient id, yet lacked an @Authorized check.\\nIts two sibling attribute readers (getPatientProgramAttributeByUuid and\\ngetPatientProgramByAttributeNameAndValue) already guard on Get Patient\\nPrograms, so this was a missed PHI read of the same class addressed by\\nGHSA-gqf9-38mg-wgqg.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Add authorization tests pinning the by-uuid program privilege checks\\n\\nThe existing tests for getPatientProgramByUuid, getPatientStateByUuid and\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName run as the privileged superuser\\nand assert only find/null behavior, so they pass even if the\\n@Authorized(Get Patient Programs) checks added by this branch are removed.\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName had no test at all.\\n\\nAdd a test per method that logs out (dropping Get Patient Programs) and\\nasserts APIAuthenticationException is thrown for otherwise-valid arguments,\\nmirroring AuthorizationAdviceTest and AdministrationServiceTest. These fail\\nif any of the three annotations is removed, pinning the fix.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f46e57d17c70440830a6ef07fde6296a79f5aed6\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T00:49:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"Require allergy privileges for getAllergies and setAllergies (#6324)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Require allergy privileges for getAllergies and setAllergies\\n\\nPatientService.getAllergies(Patient) and setAllergies(Patient, Allergies)\\ncarried no @Authorized annotation. AuthorizationAdvice only enforces when\\na method declares a privilege, so both fell through with no check at all,\\nletting any authenticated caller read or modify any patient's allergy\\nlist. The per-item siblings are already guarded (getAllergy and\\ngetAllergyByUuid require Get Allergies; saveAllergy requires Add/Edit\\nAllergies). Annotate getAllergies with Get Allergies and setAllergies with\\nAdd/Edit Allergies, and add regression tests.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Do not transitively require Get Allergies for internal allergy reads\\n\\nPR #6324 added @Authorized(GET_ALLERGIES) to PatientService.getAllergies.\\nTwo internal callers reach getAllergies through the AOP service proxy, so\\nthey now transitively demand Get Allergies from the outer caller. This is a\\nbehavior change the existing tests did not catch:\\n\\n- AllergyValidator reads the patient's existing allergies to reject a\\n  duplicate allergen whenever a new allergy is saved (allergyId == null).\\n  That runs inside saveAllergy (RequiredDataAdvice -> ValidateUtil.validate\\n  -> AllergyValidator) and on the encounter-save path, so a user holding\\n  only Add/Edit Allergies could no longer add an allergy.\\n- PatientServiceImpl.mergeAllergies reads both patients' allergies, but\\n  mergePatients is only @Authorized(EDIT_PATIENTS), so merging began to\\n  require Get Allergies as well.\\n\\nWrap each internal read in the standard addProxyPrivilege /\\nremoveProxyPrivilege idiom so the read is done on the caller's behalf\\nwithout forcing the outer operation to hold Get Allergies. The interface\\n@Authorized on getAllergies is left unchanged, so direct reads still\\nrequire the privilege.\\n\\nAdd a revert-sensitive PatientServiceTest that saves a new allergy as a\\nuser holding only Add Allergies (not Get Allergies); without the fix it\\nfails with an APIAuthenticationException for Get Allergies raised from the\\nvalidator's duplicate check.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Run the merge workflow tests as a non-super user\\n\\nmergeAndRetrieveAudit now executes mergePatients as a user who holds\\nonly the privileges the merge legitimately requires, with Get Allergies\\ndeliberately absent, so every audit-based merge workflow test guards the\\nGet Allergies proxy block in mergeAllergies: removing that block fails\\nall 27 of them with \\\"Privileges required: Get Allergies\\\".\\n\\nRunning the merge without super-user privileges surfaced one more\\ninternal read that leaked its privilege onto the caller: voiding the\\nlosing patient triggers PatientDataVoidHandler, which proxies Edit\\nCohorts for CohortService.notifyPatientVoided, but the membership read\\ninside that method goes through the service proxy and demanded Get\\nPatient Cohorts from the voiding user. That read now acquires its own\\nproxy privilege, matching the allergy reads, and the test privilege set\\nomits Get Patient Cohorts so both internal reads stay covered.\\n\\nSuggested by @ibacher during review.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d992f1746c140dc2effaf78fc86443ac35309a3c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-20T23:48:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"Bind caller-supplied names as query parameters instead of concatenating (#6335)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Bind the program-attribute name as a query parameter\\n\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName assembled its native query by\\nconcatenating the attributeName argument straight into the SQL text. Bind\\nit as a named parameter (:attributeName) instead so the value is always\\nhandled as a literal attribute-type name and can never alter the query.\\nThe patient-id list stays inlined since those elements are ints.\\n\\nAdds a regression test that a name containing SQL control characters is\\nmatched literally and resolves no attribute type.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Bind the global-property name in FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue\\n\\nReplace the concatenated global_property lookup with a PreparedStatement\\nso the property name is always treated as a literal value rather than\\nbeing spliced into the SQL text.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue name binding\\n\\nGuards that the property name is matched literally: a name carrying SQL\\ncontrol characters resolves no property (returns null) instead of being\\ninterpreted as query text, which the earlier concatenated query allowed.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c21a7cbfa2c9f67c1991372a343217e949e04f44\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T18:15:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6683: Skip full-text search with drugs when a concept is provided (#6346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"11489bdb02063ff8138f45803c336b7ef4635179\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T08:26:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6687: Improve performance of searches using the search index (#6342)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eb0a1006c7e188d4408deb298685c98ea1fef321\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T07:59:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6688: Fix circular initialization error in logging setup (#6341)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d8fe1365fbce0b4d3fc43045dff3b69ce58ca2f4\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T16:25:59+03:00\",\"message\":\"Require privileges for unprotected CohortService methods (#6317)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Require Purge Cohorts privilege for CohortService.purgeCohort\\n\\npurgeCohort permanently and irreversibly removes a cohort from the\\ndatabase but carried no @Authorized annotation, so any authenticated\\nuser could reach it through the REST purge path\\n(DELETE /ws/rest/v1/cohort/{uuid}?purge=true), even though the\\nreversible voidCohort on the same resource requires Delete Cohorts.\\nA dedicated Purge Cohorts privilege already exists in PrivilegeConstants\\nbut was never applied. Annotate purgeCohort with it, consistent with the\\nrest of the service.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for Purge Cohorts authorization\\n\\nGuards the @Authorized gate on CohortService.purgeCohort so that\\ndropping the annotation fails the build instead of silently\\nreopening the purge path to unprivileged callers.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Require Get Patient Cohorts privilege for CohortService.getCohorts\\n\\ngetCohorts(String) was the only read on the service with no\\n@Authorized, reading straight from the DAO while every sibling\\ngetter requires Get Patient Cohorts. A direct service-layer caller\\ncould therefore list cohorts (names, descriptions, member patient\\nids) with no authorization; the REST search path was only covered\\nincidentally by the resource's required-get privilege at conversion\\ntime. Gate it at the service layer to match the other getters.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Assert the specific privilege in cohort authorization tests\\n\\nCapture the thrown APIAuthenticationException and assert its message\\nnames the required privilege, so a future edit that swaps either\\nannotation to a different privilege (for purgeCohort, the exact\\nregression this PR fixes: gating on Get Patient Cohorts instead of\\nPurge Cohorts) fails the build rather than staying green.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Use containsString matcher for cohort authorization assertions\\n\\nassertThat(msg, containsString(privilege)) reports the actual message\\non failure, so a future privilege regression is self-describing in the\\nCI log instead of the bare \\\"expected true but was false\\\" that\\nassertTrue(msg.contains(..)) produces.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9c515246b4f37eafec0d6fc24de5b0455b9e3951\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T02:38:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"mergePatients does not reassign Conditions, Allergies, or MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient (#6198) (#6315)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* mergePatients now reassigns Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient\\n\\nPatientServiceImpl.mergePatients had no reassignment helpers for the\\npatient-scoped Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses tables, which\\nwere added to core after the merge logic was written. After a merge these\\nclinical records stayed attached to the now-voided non-preferred patient and\\nsilently disappeared from the surviving patient's record - a clinical-data-loss\\nand patient-safety concern (e.g. a hidden allergy).\\n\\nAdd mergeConditions, mergeAllergies and mergeMedicationDispenses helpers that\\nmove each non-voided record from the non-preferred to the preferred patient via\\nthe corresponding services, mirroring the existing\\nmergeObservationsNotContainedInEncounters pattern. Saving through the services\\nkeeps the changes audited and emits the normal save events. The moves are\\nrecorded in new PersonMergeLogData collections so they appear in the\\nPersonMergeLog.\\n\\nAllergies are deduplicated by allergen: an allergy whose allergen the preferred\\npatient already records is not moved, because a patient cannot hold two\\nallergies for the same allergen and a duplicate would make the survivor's\\nallergy list fail to load afterwards.\\n\\nFixes #6194\\n\\n\\n\\n* Keep @since on the new PersonMergeLogData accessors only, not the private fields\\n\\nThe moved* fields are private (not API and not rendered by Javadoc), so the\\nfield-level @since 2.9.0 tags were redundant. The public getters/adders keep\\n@since 2.9.0, matching the codebase convention (Patient, Condition, Allergy\\nattach @since to accessors, not backing fields).\\n\\n\\n\\n---------\\n\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 51422097a51a0918a9524ce8c0bd3aa76d17e25a)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"adec7344f655076c00cfa8ef033d998c2b8e1f5d\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T22:28:41+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6298)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6289)\\n\\nAddresses findings 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 from the sign-off issue:\\n\\n- Finding 1: OutboxEventRegistry now triggers scheduler when listeners are\\n  found, replacing the SmartInitializingSingleton in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer.\\n  Adds registerBean() so modules can register listeners at runtime.\\n- Finding 2: Use Context.loadClass() instead of Class.forName() in\\n  OutboxPollingTaskHandler so module-defined event types resolve correctly.\\n- Finding 4: Change outbox_event.payload and completed_listeners columns\\n  from TEXT to MEDIUMTEXT in both the update changelog and schema-only snapshot;\\n  align OutboxEvent entity columnDefinition to match.\\n- Finding 5: BrokerEventListenerFactory now rejects BrokerIncomingEvent<?>\\n  (wildcard/raw) at registration time with a clear error instead of silently\\n  wiring a consumer that dead-letters every message.\\n- Finding 7: Document on OpenmrsServiceEventAdvice that a synchronous\\n  @EventListener exception aborting the service call is intentional.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix getMaximumPropertyLength to treat MEDIUMTEXT/TEXT/CLOB as unbounded\\n\\nOnly LONGTEXT was special-cased to return Integer.MAX_VALUE; MEDIUMTEXT\\nand other LOB-like types fell through to column.getLength() (default 255),\\ncausing ValidateUtil to reject payloads that fit the actual DB column.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix tests broken by Finding 1 and Finding 5 refactors\\n\\n- OutboxEventIT: afterSingletonsInstantiated() renamed to schedule()\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: raw BrokerIncomingEvent -> BrokerIncomingEvent<String>\\n  to comply with the new fail-fast check for wildcard types\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix two test failures caused by Finding 4 and Finding 5 fixes\\n\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: publish BrokerIncomingEvent<String> with a\\n  payload so getResolvableType() resolves to the concrete generic type\\n  and Spring's listener type-matching accepts it against the\\n  BrokerIncomingEvent<String> method parameter.\\n- HibernateAdministrationDAO: scope the MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT unbounded\\n  treatment to only those two explicit columnDefinition values; remove\\n  CLOB since @Lob fields without columnDefinition map to CLOB in H2,\\n  which would suppress the 64 KB TEXT length check in\\n  BaseAttributeTypeValidatorTest.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Revise BrokerIncomingEvent/OutgoingEvent header docs and fix test\\n\\n* Address PR review comments on #6298\\n\\n- Restore deleteScheduledTasks() in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer and call\\n  it from OutboxEventRegistry when disabled or no listeners found, so JobRunr\\n  jobs don't keep firing after the last listener module is uninstalled\\n- Drop registerBean(): ModuleUtil.refreshApplicationContext re-runs\\n  afterSingletonsInstantiated() on module start, so module listeners are\\n  picked up without any module-side call\\n- Add String payloads to all three BrokerEventListenerTest events so\\n  getResolvableType() resolves to BrokerIncomingEvent<String> and filter\\n  tests actually exercise the source/broker filter logic\\n- Add wildcard BrokerIncomingEvent<?> test case to BrokerEventListenerFactoryTest\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00\",\"message\":\"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"rkorytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c4aca3af4154dc99969cb6aed48a1e71c9a70055\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T11:17:09+02:00\",\"message\":\"Porting TRUNK-6429 and TRUNK-6515 to master (#6233)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6429: Create application events for service method calls and entity changes (#6084)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 144fee399f79b7152f2fcbaade069a7cfd3285e3)\\n\\n* TRUNK-6516: Provide CDC mechanism with Debezium (#6151)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 57f4018ffbcdb27dac86677ca2791d9fae6cfc89)\\n\\n* TRUNK-6429: Addressing post commit review (#6190)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit a4331e297c2ad33b9d615174f7b6e52b26ef236c)\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b8e70f6a839fd77c9d396b2f40b83064d88498b2\",\"date\":\"2026-06-25T00:33:14+03:00\",\"message\":\"Use PipeParser for inbound HL7 to remove XML/XXE attack surface (#6223)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The hL7Parser bean was a HAPI GenericParser, which auto-detects message\\nencoding and routes XML-encoded payloads to HAPI's XML parser. That XML\\nparser can expose XML external entity (XXE) processing - external file\\nreads, SSRF and entity-expansion DoS - when its underlying JAXP factory is\\nnot hardened. OpenMRS only ever produces and consumes pipe-delimited (ER7)\\nHL7v2 messages, so the XML branch is unused attack surface.\\n\\nSwitch the bean to a PipeParser, which rejects XML payloads outright with\\nan unsupported-encoding error. The HL7ServiceImpl parser field and setter\\nare widened to the common Parser supertype so injection still resolves and\\nexisting setParser callers remain source-compatible.\\n\\nAdds a regression test asserting an XML/DOCTYPE/external-entity payload is\\nrefused before any XML processing occurs.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b3a2fa0b2d45c31065f89651f4f9801aa45354b4\",\"date\":\"2026-06-01T17:21:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria, (#6079)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria,\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* add support for searching by concept name; fix test\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* misc styling\\n\\n* change since version to 2.8.7; address feedback\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to ConceptReferenceTerm\\n\\n* switch to addUuids(String... uuids) and addConceptId(Integer... conceptIds)\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"11607283d6100942c99bcdbb6713352f62c0b53a\",\"date\":\"2026-05-18T12:09:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find … (#6088)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find descendent Locations efficiently\\n\\n* coderabbit suggestions\\n\\n* style\\n\\n* address feedback (with more efficient queries)\\n\\n* make LocationSearchCriteria take Location and LocationTag types instead of uuids\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to Location.tags to optimize location.getTags() calls\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* forward-port changes from #6089\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"22a4bae33c93d5a235cac846a440940733a5ce42\",\"date\":\"2026-04-14T14:00:17-04:00\",\"message\":\"Fix admin_password_locked implementation\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":44}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cbe038f-9f62-4368-916e-b7e56f4e6014","uuid":"6e945e4a-193b-4fb8-8d9d-5a469aef1aad","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:09:57.713Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"5eb8cba2e30befeaec8ab7892dff14ac7dcc9d87\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:37:18+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException (#6674)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD, origin/master, origin/HEAD, master\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException\\n\\nSince TRUNK-6799, AuthorizationAdvice and core's explicit privilege\\nchecks denied with Spring Security's AccessDeniedException rather than\\nAPIAuthenticationException. Code catching the old type stopped\\nrecognizing denials; webservices.rest maps only that type, so REST\\nanswered 500 where it answered 401 or 403.\\n\\nAPIAuthenticationException now extends AuthorizationDeniedException.\\nCore throws it again wherever it did before 3.0.0, and wherever a\\n@PreAuthorize or @PostAuthorize check names the missing privilege, so a\\ncatch on either type recognizes the denial. It stays deprecated in\\nfavour of AccessDeniedException, which every denial is.\\n\\nIt is no longer an APIException, so a module compiled against an earlier\\ncore whose bytecode treats it as one fails verification until rebuilt.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6823: Deny a failed isAuthenticated() with APIAuthenticationException too\\n\\n@PreAuthorize(\\\"isAuthenticated()\\\"), the migration guide's translation of a\\nno-value @Authorized, denied a logged-out caller with a plain\\nAuthorizationDeniedException where @Authorized throws\\nAPIAuthenticationException, so converting such a method changed what its\\ncallers catch. It now records the denial for\\nPrivilegeNamingAuthorizationManager to report as AuthorizationAdvice does.\\n\\nTestInstallUtil throws APIAuthenticationException again, as before 3.0.0,\\nand the migration guide notes that the class is no longer an APIException.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0e0255b872f08dabafe9414d623820272cd475be\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:24:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6827: Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor (#6637)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor\\n\\nFixes #6636\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Keep the outbox from enqueueing events about its own rows\\n\\nNow that onPersist reaches EventInterceptor, saving an OutboxEvent row\\npublishes a SaveDbEvent about that row. With an @OutboxEventListener\\nthat accepts it, such as one taking SaveDbEvent<?> or EntityEvent<?>,\\nOutboxEventInterceptor saved another OutboxEvent for it, and so on,\\nuntil the JVM ran out of heap on the first create or update.\\nOutboxEventInterceptor now ignores entity events whose entity is an\\nOutboxEvent.\\n\\nThe new ChainingInterceptor overrides are @since 3.0.0, because 2.9.x\\nbuilds against Hibernate 5.6, whose Interceptor has no onPersist or\\nonRemove.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Stop auditing OutboxEvent with Envers\\n\\nWith hibernate.integration.envers.enabled=true, Envers writes the audit\\nrow of each new or changed OutboxEvent just before the transaction\\ncommits, with persist(entityName, Map). The SaveDbEvent for that row has\\na HashMap as its entity, so the OutboxEvent check in\\nOutboxEventInterceptor let it through to a listener such as one taking\\nSaveDbEvent<?>. That saved another OutboxEvent, whose audit row came\\nnext, and so on, with each payload nesting the previous one. On H2 the\\ncommit ended in OutOfMemoryError. On MySQL it ended in \\\"Data too long\\nfor column 'payload'\\\", so logins and the outbox poller failed.\\n\\nOutboxEvent is no longer @Audited, as on 2.9.x.\\nEnversAuditTableInitializerDatabaseIT expected an audit table for every\\nentity with an @Audited superclass, but Envers does not audit\\nOutboxEvent through BaseOpenmrsObject's annotation, so the test now\\nchecks the entity's own annotation.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"cb6cda4236b21a84cc4e1765a0dbaa58fdbe2565\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T15:17:25+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6802 Extend hasPermission to support custom rules provided from modules (#6668)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0340ada6bd4209e38630ebe7978041e0b514f85c\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T14:08:49+03:00\",\"message\":\"Initialize Context's user context holder before its logger (#6672)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes #6670\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"83411b2f8a52325e867fccc223a54d6a6f701400\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T22:20:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6819: Start the JobRunr job server only once OpenMRS has started (#6654)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The background job server was started while its application context was\\nstill being created, so jobs could run before the context was ready. On\\njetty:run this logged \\\"EntityManagerFactory is closed\\\" for a job that ran\\nduring the context refresh after modules start, against the closed session\\nfactory of the context being replaced, and \\\"Task class ... not found\\\" for a\\nmodule's job that ran after the first, core-only refresh, before modules\\nwere loaded.\\n\\nThe server is now started by a SmartLifecycle once its context has finished\\nrefreshing and stopped before the context closes. The webapp defers that\\nstart until SchedulerService.onStartup(), which runs once modules have\\nstarted; contexts refreshed after startup start their server right away.\\n\\nThe webapp never closes its application context, so Context.shutdown() now\\ncalls SchedulerService.onShutdown() first, as it did before the move to\\nJobRunr, and JobRunrSchedulerService stops the job server there, before the\\nmodules and the session factory are shut down.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NK4kFG8qyevx9Bk9jWoEgS\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PdDdZrB8Q5eMgej5FmRx4R\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZ92BDLHrn6xACczVMtSiR\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"41c5821a9b8b2d184207c8842e4c4331e02aaa7f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T21:27:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType (#6633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType\\n\\nFixes #6632\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Document that modules map their enums with StringEnumType\\n\\nThe class Javadoc said to delete StringEnumType once Obs, ConceptName\\nand OrderSet move to annotations. Modules now map their own enums with\\nit, so say that instead.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ja9UqKCQ2eMd7FaYQ2ewqz\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b64e0729cce60c40dffb75788c4b43937a6fc77e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T08:23:37-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6818: Context.closeSession() closes sessions it did not open (#6651)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2c9b2ee0dd005f64fa543ca8228c51f57cb319c7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T10:15:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6810: Extend cluster-safety to RolePrivilegeCache (#6627)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"07e8ea06f244de96907581535d4eff8dadbd0004\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:26:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6707: Implement full caching for Global Properties (#6598)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b147e0dcae701feb4670b53a454daf0cfb210ee9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T16:07:23+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6684: Location.childLocations gained unintended orphanRemoval=true in the JPA migration (#6444)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Wikum Weerakutti <wikum@linuxdeveloper.space>\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f10e3fb9a645378ab6682c21d6be478bfdab6199\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T16:28:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6721: Replace StackWalker with a thread-local guard in UserDAO (#6588)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"34bd26a8166d1277f83e4fdf1bda550ff8cc49a6\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T22:26:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6686: Restore relevance weighting in patient search lost in the Hibernate Search 6 migration (#6430)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3310bc1d9682151ac461faf0916ca3da7d5a88d0\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T14:06:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Follow-up: Re-add null privilege check and add guards\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1d0fb13892759020f6bc0824a097518d546024eb\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T13:45:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Reduce the overhead of the gzip filter (#6505)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6d787a1e60899e39377ce5011b298a188b3354c6\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T13:54:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6780: Add a MariaDB option to the test container harness (#6474)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit 5983a2b85e60caf1fdf7edaa8abc860d9f1dd17d)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6e77bfd03ab134fc7d66a0e3140d6e468f569ec5\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T11:39:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6697: HandlerUtil's cache should not be garbage collected (#6494)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ac1bd8778fc13247eb712a6cd7a949461cccdb6b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T07:58:28-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6662: Get unchanged password hashing working using Spring's interfaces (#6219)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit d58b63501b7fedd1e6b02981262d73122b967621)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d92b490aaa25fbd255be0d08a04da4772a03e3b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-22T01:13:29+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6756: Remove deprecated Daemon thread-execution overloads (#6483)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"tejas\",\"authorEmail\":\"tejaswaghmare.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d222c6085bbe13f62be68908ad9c3abbaa75db1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T12:44:57-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6729:  Let batch loading engage on the identifier and concept search paths (#6420)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Rohith Gurram\",\"authorEmail\":\"89861100+Rocker810@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2ce847744295132bbe5fb97f369fab714f09b309\",\"date\":\"2026-08-20T19:57:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6731: Add paging support to the obs retrieval API (#6410)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8bb5c2e9e36ab8fb09f0053786bc0f040775cc1e\",\"date\":\"2026-08-11T20:49:53+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6733: Use java-uuid-generator for entity UUIDs instead of UUID.randomUUID() (#6391)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Sathieskumar Sudeshkar\",\"authorEmail\":\"sudeshkar008sk@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1b5421a9a8d69030adb91124c3f9cb758dbc58a8\",\"date\":\"2026-07-24T11:14:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6712: Cache flattened role privileges for privilege and superuser checks (#6383)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"befcc055a108c28458fc21ff73f07dfe844f78a4\",\"date\":\"2026-07-24T10:16:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"Improve test suite run time (#6377)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1f6cc621cb7bf97dc4283b0c808f96373d90054f\",\"date\":\"2026-07-22T15:41:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6711: Batch-load search result pages (#6363)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9e011e2c09db99fd5cae20821e203fe9cc5f036b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T23:50:01+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6681: Improve LocationSearchCriteria query performance with pagination (#6359)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"omeri innocent\",\"authorEmail\":\"innocentomeri08@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"265582974b2589ffc8787b57c2e4ba0368cb6cba\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T12:44:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6713: Follow-up: Comment clean-up\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This was already included in the backports\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b68355b3dd934c7d5be3708d6637dfae8f845ee5\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T11:26:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6713: Switch to saner DaemonThread protection scheme (#6349)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"41ec2955656c6d7131c628d122d8c503b09c4cb1\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T10:37:09-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6694 & TRUNK-6695: Avoid synchronization in service fetching (#6348)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"50810cfb4d919602fa727eb78607675e2a5e3ec0\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T01:25:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"Require Get Patient Programs privilege for by-uuid program lookups (#6318)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Require Get Patient Programs privilege for by-uuid program lookups\\n\\nProgramWorkflowService.getPatientProgramByUuid and getPatientStateByUuid\\nhad no @Authorized annotation. Because AuthorizationAdvice only enforces\\nwhen a method declares a privilege, both fell through with no check at\\nall, letting any authenticated user read program-enrollment PHI by uuid.\\nEvery other read on the service, including getPatientProgram(Integer),\\nalready requires Get Patient Programs; annotate both by-uuid methods to\\nmatch.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Require Get Patient Programs privilege for patient program attribute lookup\\n\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName returns patient program\\nattribute values keyed by patient id, yet lacked an @Authorized check.\\nIts two sibling attribute readers (getPatientProgramAttributeByUuid and\\ngetPatientProgramByAttributeNameAndValue) already guard on Get Patient\\nPrograms, so this was a missed PHI read of the same class addressed by\\nGHSA-gqf9-38mg-wgqg.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Add authorization tests pinning the by-uuid program privilege checks\\n\\nThe existing tests for getPatientProgramByUuid, getPatientStateByUuid and\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName run as the privileged superuser\\nand assert only find/null behavior, so they pass even if the\\n@Authorized(Get Patient Programs) checks added by this branch are removed.\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName had no test at all.\\n\\nAdd a test per method that logs out (dropping Get Patient Programs) and\\nasserts APIAuthenticationException is thrown for otherwise-valid arguments,\\nmirroring AuthorizationAdviceTest and AdministrationServiceTest. These fail\\nif any of the three annotations is removed, pinning the fix.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f46e57d17c70440830a6ef07fde6296a79f5aed6\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T00:49:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"Require allergy privileges for getAllergies and setAllergies (#6324)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Require allergy privileges for getAllergies and setAllergies\\n\\nPatientService.getAllergies(Patient) and setAllergies(Patient, Allergies)\\ncarried no @Authorized annotation. AuthorizationAdvice only enforces when\\na method declares a privilege, so both fell through with no check at all,\\nletting any authenticated caller read or modify any patient's allergy\\nlist. The per-item siblings are already guarded (getAllergy and\\ngetAllergyByUuid require Get Allergies; saveAllergy requires Add/Edit\\nAllergies). Annotate getAllergies with Get Allergies and setAllergies with\\nAdd/Edit Allergies, and add regression tests.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Do not transitively require Get Allergies for internal allergy reads\\n\\nPR #6324 added @Authorized(GET_ALLERGIES) to PatientService.getAllergies.\\nTwo internal callers reach getAllergies through the AOP service proxy, so\\nthey now transitively demand Get Allergies from the outer caller. This is a\\nbehavior change the existing tests did not catch:\\n\\n- AllergyValidator reads the patient's existing allergies to reject a\\n  duplicate allergen whenever a new allergy is saved (allergyId == null).\\n  That runs inside saveAllergy (RequiredDataAdvice -> ValidateUtil.validate\\n  -> AllergyValidator) and on the encounter-save path, so a user holding\\n  only Add/Edit Allergies could no longer add an allergy.\\n- PatientServiceImpl.mergeAllergies reads both patients' allergies, but\\n  mergePatients is only @Authorized(EDIT_PATIENTS), so merging began to\\n  require Get Allergies as well.\\n\\nWrap each internal read in the standard addProxyPrivilege /\\nremoveProxyPrivilege idiom so the read is done on the caller's behalf\\nwithout forcing the outer operation to hold Get Allergies. The interface\\n@Authorized on getAllergies is left unchanged, so direct reads still\\nrequire the privilege.\\n\\nAdd a revert-sensitive PatientServiceTest that saves a new allergy as a\\nuser holding only Add Allergies (not Get Allergies); without the fix it\\nfails with an APIAuthenticationException for Get Allergies raised from the\\nvalidator's duplicate check.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Run the merge workflow tests as a non-super user\\n\\nmergeAndRetrieveAudit now executes mergePatients as a user who holds\\nonly the privileges the merge legitimately requires, with Get Allergies\\ndeliberately absent, so every audit-based merge workflow test guards the\\nGet Allergies proxy block in mergeAllergies: removing that block fails\\nall 27 of them with \\\"Privileges required: Get Allergies\\\".\\n\\nRunning the merge without super-user privileges surfaced one more\\ninternal read that leaked its privilege onto the caller: voiding the\\nlosing patient triggers PatientDataVoidHandler, which proxies Edit\\nCohorts for CohortService.notifyPatientVoided, but the membership read\\ninside that method goes through the service proxy and demanded Get\\nPatient Cohorts from the voiding user. That read now acquires its own\\nproxy privilege, matching the allergy reads, and the test privilege set\\nomits Get Patient Cohorts so both internal reads stay covered.\\n\\nSuggested by @ibacher during review.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d992f1746c140dc2effaf78fc86443ac35309a3c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-20T23:48:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"Bind caller-supplied names as query parameters instead of concatenating (#6335)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Bind the program-attribute name as a query parameter\\n\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName assembled its native query by\\nconcatenating the attributeName argument straight into the SQL text. Bind\\nit as a named parameter (:attributeName) instead so the value is always\\nhandled as a literal attribute-type name and can never alter the query.\\nThe patient-id list stays inlined since those elements are ints.\\n\\nAdds a regression test that a name containing SQL control characters is\\nmatched literally and resolves no attribute type.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Bind the global-property name in FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue\\n\\nReplace the concatenated global_property lookup with a PreparedStatement\\nso the property name is always treated as a literal value rather than\\nbeing spliced into the SQL text.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue name binding\\n\\nGuards that the property name is matched literally: a name carrying SQL\\ncontrol characters resolves no property (returns null) instead of being\\ninterpreted as query text, which the earlier concatenated query allowed.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c21a7cbfa2c9f67c1991372a343217e949e04f44\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T18:15:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6683: Skip full-text search with drugs when a concept is provided (#6346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"11489bdb02063ff8138f45803c336b7ef4635179\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T08:26:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6687: Improve performance of searches using the search index (#6342)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eb0a1006c7e188d4408deb298685c98ea1fef321\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T07:59:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6688: Fix circular initialization error in logging setup (#6341)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d8fe1365fbce0b4d3fc43045dff3b69ce58ca2f4\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T16:25:59+03:00\",\"message\":\"Require privileges for unprotected CohortService methods (#6317)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Require Purge Cohorts privilege for CohortService.purgeCohort\\n\\npurgeCohort permanently and irreversibly removes a cohort from the\\ndatabase but carried no @Authorized annotation, so any authenticated\\nuser could reach it through the REST purge path\\n(DELETE /ws/rest/v1/cohort/{uuid}?purge=true), even though the\\nreversible voidCohort on the same resource requires Delete Cohorts.\\nA dedicated Purge Cohorts privilege already exists in PrivilegeConstants\\nbut was never applied. Annotate purgeCohort with it, consistent with the\\nrest of the service.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for Purge Cohorts authorization\\n\\nGuards the @Authorized gate on CohortService.purgeCohort so that\\ndropping the annotation fails the build instead of silently\\nreopening the purge path to unprivileged callers.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Require Get Patient Cohorts privilege for CohortService.getCohorts\\n\\ngetCohorts(String) was the only read on the service with no\\n@Authorized, reading straight from the DAO while every sibling\\ngetter requires Get Patient Cohorts. A direct service-layer caller\\ncould therefore list cohorts (names, descriptions, member patient\\nids) with no authorization; the REST search path was only covered\\nincidentally by the resource's required-get privilege at conversion\\ntime. Gate it at the service layer to match the other getters.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Assert the specific privilege in cohort authorization tests\\n\\nCapture the thrown APIAuthenticationException and assert its message\\nnames the required privilege, so a future edit that swaps either\\nannotation to a different privilege (for purgeCohort, the exact\\nregression this PR fixes: gating on Get Patient Cohorts instead of\\nPurge Cohorts) fails the build rather than staying green.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Use containsString matcher for cohort authorization assertions\\n\\nassertThat(msg, containsString(privilege)) reports the actual message\\non failure, so a future privilege regression is self-describing in the\\nCI log instead of the bare \\\"expected true but was false\\\" that\\nassertTrue(msg.contains(..)) produces.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9c515246b4f37eafec0d6fc24de5b0455b9e3951\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T02:38:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"mergePatients does not reassign Conditions, Allergies, or MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient (#6198) (#6315)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* mergePatients now reassigns Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient\\n\\nPatientServiceImpl.mergePatients had no reassignment helpers for the\\npatient-scoped Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses tables, which\\nwere added to core after the merge logic was written. After a merge these\\nclinical records stayed attached to the now-voided non-preferred patient and\\nsilently disappeared from the surviving patient's record - a clinical-data-loss\\nand patient-safety concern (e.g. a hidden allergy).\\n\\nAdd mergeConditions, mergeAllergies and mergeMedicationDispenses helpers that\\nmove each non-voided record from the non-preferred to the preferred patient via\\nthe corresponding services, mirroring the existing\\nmergeObservationsNotContainedInEncounters pattern. Saving through the services\\nkeeps the changes audited and emits the normal save events. The moves are\\nrecorded in new PersonMergeLogData collections so they appear in the\\nPersonMergeLog.\\n\\nAllergies are deduplicated by allergen: an allergy whose allergen the preferred\\npatient already records is not moved, because a patient cannot hold two\\nallergies for the same allergen and a duplicate would make the survivor's\\nallergy list fail to load afterwards.\\n\\nFixes #6194\\n\\n\\n\\n* Keep @since on the new PersonMergeLogData accessors only, not the private fields\\n\\nThe moved* fields are private (not API and not rendered by Javadoc), so the\\nfield-level @since 2.9.0 tags were redundant. The public getters/adders keep\\n@since 2.9.0, matching the codebase convention (Patient, Condition, Allergy\\nattach @since to accessors, not backing fields).\\n\\n\\n\\n---------\\n\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 51422097a51a0918a9524ce8c0bd3aa76d17e25a)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"adec7344f655076c00cfa8ef033d998c2b8e1f5d\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T22:28:41+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6298)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6289)\\n\\nAddresses findings 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 from the sign-off issue:\\n\\n- Finding 1: OutboxEventRegistry now triggers scheduler when listeners are\\n  found, replacing the SmartInitializingSingleton in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer.\\n  Adds registerBean() so modules can register listeners at runtime.\\n- Finding 2: Use Context.loadClass() instead of Class.forName() in\\n  OutboxPollingTaskHandler so module-defined event types resolve correctly.\\n- Finding 4: Change outbox_event.payload and completed_listeners columns\\n  from TEXT to MEDIUMTEXT in both the update changelog and schema-only snapshot;\\n  align OutboxEvent entity columnDefinition to match.\\n- Finding 5: BrokerEventListenerFactory now rejects BrokerIncomingEvent<?>\\n  (wildcard/raw) at registration time with a clear error instead of silently\\n  wiring a consumer that dead-letters every message.\\n- Finding 7: Document on OpenmrsServiceEventAdvice that a synchronous\\n  @EventListener exception aborting the service call is intentional.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix getMaximumPropertyLength to treat MEDIUMTEXT/TEXT/CLOB as unbounded\\n\\nOnly LONGTEXT was special-cased to return Integer.MAX_VALUE; MEDIUMTEXT\\nand other LOB-like types fell through to column.getLength() (default 255),\\ncausing ValidateUtil to reject payloads that fit the actual DB column.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix tests broken by Finding 1 and Finding 5 refactors\\n\\n- OutboxEventIT: afterSingletonsInstantiated() renamed to schedule()\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: raw BrokerIncomingEvent -> BrokerIncomingEvent<String>\\n  to comply with the new fail-fast check for wildcard types\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix two test failures caused by Finding 4 and Finding 5 fixes\\n\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: publish BrokerIncomingEvent<String> with a\\n  payload so getResolvableType() resolves to the concrete generic type\\n  and Spring's listener type-matching accepts it against the\\n  BrokerIncomingEvent<String> method parameter.\\n- HibernateAdministrationDAO: scope the MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT unbounded\\n  treatment to only those two explicit columnDefinition values; remove\\n  CLOB since @Lob fields without columnDefinition map to CLOB in H2,\\n  which would suppress the 64 KB TEXT length check in\\n  BaseAttributeTypeValidatorTest.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Revise BrokerIncomingEvent/OutgoingEvent header docs and fix test\\n\\n* Address PR review comments on #6298\\n\\n- Restore deleteScheduledTasks() in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer and call\\n  it from OutboxEventRegistry when disabled or no listeners found, so JobRunr\\n  jobs don't keep firing after the last listener module is uninstalled\\n- Drop registerBean(): ModuleUtil.refreshApplicationContext re-runs\\n  afterSingletonsInstantiated() on module start, so module listeners are\\n  picked up without any module-side call\\n- Add String payloads to all three BrokerEventListenerTest events so\\n  getResolvableType() resolves to BrokerIncomingEvent<String> and filter\\n  tests actually exercise the source/broker filter logic\\n- Add wildcard BrokerIncomingEvent<?> test case to BrokerEventListenerFactoryTest\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00\",\"message\":\"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"rkorytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c4aca3af4154dc99969cb6aed48a1e71c9a70055\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T11:17:09+02:00\",\"message\":\"Porting TRUNK-6429 and TRUNK-6515 to master (#6233)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6429: Create application events for service method calls and entity changes (#6084)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 144fee399f79b7152f2fcbaade069a7cfd3285e3)\\n\\n* TRUNK-6516: Provide CDC mechanism with Debezium (#6151)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 57f4018ffbcdb27dac86677ca2791d9fae6cfc89)\\n\\n* TRUNK-6429: Addressing post commit review (#6190)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit a4331e297c2ad33b9d615174f7b6e52b26ef236c)\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b8e70f6a839fd77c9d396b2f40b83064d88498b2\",\"date\":\"2026-06-25T00:33:14+03:00\",\"message\":\"Use PipeParser for inbound HL7 to remove XML/XXE attack surface (#6223)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The hL7Parser bean was a HAPI GenericParser, which auto-detects message\\nencoding and routes XML-encoded payloads to HAPI's XML parser. That XML\\nparser can expose XML external entity (XXE) processing - external file\\nreads, SSRF and entity-expansion DoS - when its underlying JAXP factory is\\nnot hardened. OpenMRS only ever produces and consumes pipe-delimited (ER7)\\nHL7v2 messages, so the XML branch is unused attack surface.\\n\\nSwitch the bean to a PipeParser, which rejects XML payloads outright with\\nan unsupported-encoding error. The HL7ServiceImpl parser field and setter\\nare widened to the common Parser supertype so injection still resolves and\\nexisting setParser callers remain source-compatible.\\n\\nAdds a regression test asserting an XML/DOCTYPE/external-entity payload is\\nrefused before any XML processing occurs.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b3a2fa0b2d45c31065f89651f4f9801aa45354b4\",\"date\":\"2026-06-01T17:21:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria, (#6079)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria,\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* add support for searching by concept name; fix test\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* misc styling\\n\\n* change since version to 2.8.7; address feedback\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to ConceptReferenceTerm\\n\\n* switch to addUuids(String... uuids) and addConceptId(Integer... conceptIds)\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"11607283d6100942c99bcdbb6713352f62c0b53a\",\"date\":\"2026-05-18T12:09:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find … (#6088)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find descendent Locations efficiently\\n\\n* coderabbit suggestions\\n\\n* style\\n\\n* address feedback (with more efficient queries)\\n\\n* make LocationSearchCriteria take Location and LocationTag types instead of uuids\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to Location.tags to optimize location.getTags() calls\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* forward-port changes from #6089\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"22a4bae33c93d5a235cac846a440940733a5ce42\",\"date\":\"2026-04-14T14:00:17-04:00\",\"message\":\"Fix admin_password_locked implementation\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":44}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BgP6sm7dV9sRVJBXD1wJVb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
